From 31212d85eb65236f1236507fbf41c7542d4606b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigel Shearman <georgemog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:18:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] zz9000: hardware bring-up fixes, test tools, benchmark
 results

Brought up on the MiSTer with the A4091+RTG+A2065 v2 core; all three
depths now pass a pixel-exact comparison against the native blitter.

Fixes found on hardware:
- exec CacheClearU() does not flush the FPGA CPU cache: cpu_cache_new
  clears on a 0->1 edge of CACR bit 3 and the TG68 latches it, so only
  the first call after a CacheControl() clears. The first kick read a
  stale DONE, timed out and disabled acceleration. New
  mister_fpga_cache_clear() toggles CI 0->1 in supervisor mode with chip
  reads in between so the controller samples both levels.
- service thread inherited MiSTer's CPU1 affinity and fought the busy
  main loop (flat ~0.5ms/op); pin it to CPU0 -> ~1.75x throughput.
- P96 board name back to "MiSTer" so Picasso96Settings modes carry over.
- protocol v2: DONE ring on separate cache lines, one flush per op.

Added MiSTerZZTest (accelerated scene vs planar reference + benchmark),
SetToolType (set BOARDTYPE from the CLI), driver diagnostics in spare
mailbox words, shown by MiSTerZZInfo.

Benchmarks vs software MiSTer.card: big fills 4-6x, scrolls 3-4x, text
1.5-1.8x, small fills 1.5-3x, short lines ~0.85x.

